Mimara's owner during her first five years in Carythusal.The mortal daughter of Gilgaöl in ancient Sakarpi legend, remembered in a tale involving the Sakarpi king Suberd.The Norsirai king of Atrithau and last ruler in the line of Morghund. His name is the Sheyic form of Athullara.The High-Priestess of the Cult of Yatwer.A captain in the Imperial Army and follower of Ikurei Conphas.A Siölan Cûnuroi, wife of Cinial'jin and presumed mother of Immiriccas, Aisralu, and Enpiralas.A Siölan Cûnuroi, daughter of Cinial'jin and presumed daughter of Aisarinqu; Immiriccas and Enpiralas are her brothers.A Ketyai philosopher born in Mehtsonc, celebrated as the father of syllogistic logic and algebra and regarded by many as the greatest philosopher. His critical philosophy has a consistently skeptical core, questioning beliefs founded on human weakness rather than reason or the world. Recognized as a prodigy, he received the Kyranean institution of Protection from the High King at eight years old, granting him freedom to speak without fear of reprisal. His writings include The Syllogistics, Meta-Analytics, Theophysics, and several Analytics of Men.The god of thievery and deception, represented in scripture as either a mischievous companion or a cruel rival of other gods. Although named among the primary Gods in The Chronicle of the Tusk, he has no formal cult; his devotees instead form an informal network across the great cities of the Three Seas. The Mar’eddat names him as Gierra's faithless husband.The god of disease and a Bellicose God who favors those who struggle against his influence rather than flatterers and worshippers. His priesthood is consequently the Three Seas' principal repository of physicians. Its priests employ pharmaka and reliquaries against illness, sound small prayer chimes in thanks, and may bear devotional tattoos.The Ketyai Palatine of Kutapileth in High Ainon and one of the leaders of the Vulgar Holy War.An elderly Cironji Ketyai who serves as body-slave to Prince Nersei Proyas.A Kûniüric lord who took part in the Second Ordeal at the Battle of Eleneöt Fields.One of Esmenet's body-slaves.A legendary Surartu Grandmaster of the Scarlet Spires, responsible for securing the river fortress of Kiz in Far Antique Carythusal.A Ketyai nobleman who holds the Conriyan title of Palatine of Ankirioth.The goddess of fortune and one of the principal Compensatory Gods, rewarding mortal devotion with paradise in the afterlife. Her cult is especially popular among the higher political castes of the Three Seas. Old Kiünnat tradition calls her the younger sister of Bukris, god of famine, and she is also associated with the stars and favorable conjunctions.A presumably mythical figure mentioned in one of the Boatman's songs.The last and greatest High King of Kûniüri and leader of the coalition against Golgotterath during the early Apocalypse. A close friend of the sorcerer Seswatha, who often advised him, he was married to Suriala and counted Ganrelka II and the renowned warrior Nau-Cayûti among his sons. He wielded Glimir, a large ensorcelled sword said to pass through foes with ease.The heir and successor of Anasûrimbor Celmomas II, a participant in the Second Ordeal, and the last reigning High King of Kûniüri.A Norsirai of Kûniüri and the twin brother of Anasûrimbor Celmomas II, remembered in The Sagas.A Prince-Imperial of the New Empire and a child of Kellhus and Esmenet.The first son and eldest child of Kellhus and Esmenet, a Prince-Imperial and General of the Kidruhil. Born in Shimeh and named for Anasûrimbor Nau-Cayûti, he was raised alongside Moënghus II as a fraternal twin. Tall and slender, with blond hair, blue eyes, a long face, and a plaited beard, he closely resembles his father.A Norsirai Dûnyain monk of the Anasûrimbor line, known as the Prince of Nothing and identified as the son of Anasûrimbor Moënghus.A Prince-Imperial of the New Empire, the third son and sixth child of Kellhus and Esmenet, and the twin brother of Samarmas. Half Dûnyain and half Ketyai, he was named after Anasûrimbor Celmomas II.A Norsirai Dûnyain monk.A Norsirai former Dûnyain monk and the father of Anasûrimbor Kellhus.The eldest of the Prince-Imperials and the son of Serwë.A famed Norsirai High King of Aörsi whose deeds are recounted in The Sagas.A High King of Aörsi who commissioned the fortress of Dagliash.The first Anasûrimbor High King and founder of Kûniüri, established after his defeat of the Scintya. His Kûniüric epithet derives from the Ûmeritic nanar hukisha. He expanded Kûniüri from the Yimaleti Mountains to the Cerish Sea and from Sakarpus to the Demua Mountains, beginning what scholars regard as the longest-reigning dynasty in recorded history.A High King of Aörsi who ordered the abandonment of all ninety-nine Hooded Redoubts.A prince of Kûniüri, the youngest son of Celmomas II and Suriala, and a hero celebrated in The Sagas.A Norsirai High King of ancient Aörsi during the era of the Apocalypse.A Norsirai woman of the Ûmeri Empire, the first daughter of Sanna-Neorjë of House Anasûrimbor and mother of Sanna-Jephera.A Prince-Imperial of the New Empire, the fourth son and seventh and youngest child of Kellhus and Esmenet, and the twin brother of Kelmomas. He is half Dûnyain and half Ketyai.An Ûmeri Man–Nonman hybrid, son of Anasûrimbor Omindalea and the Nonman Siqû Jiricet. He was formally adopted as the heir of his grandfather, Anasûrimbor Sanna-Neorjë.A Norsirai nobleman who headed House Anasûrimbor in the Ûmeri Empire. He was the father of Omindalea and formally adopted his grandson Sanna-Jephera as his heir.A Princess-Imperial of the New Empire, the second daughter and third child of Kellhus and Esmenet. Named after Serwë, she is Grandmistress of the Swayal Sisterhood, the only school for sorceresses in Eärwa.A half-Dûnyain, half-Ketyai Princess-Imperial of the New Empire, the eldest daughter and second child of Kellhus and Esmenet. She serves as an Imperial Adviser in Momemn.A Ketyai High King of Kyraneas during the Apocalypse and a close friend of the sorcerer Seswatha, who called him Anakka. He was entrusted with the Heron Spear, a weapon central to the struggle against the No-God.The artist who created the celebrated fresco known as the Blue Hubris.The most celebrated Old Prophet of the Tusk, credited with leading the Five Tribes of Men into Eärwa. He is called the Burnt Prophet because, when confronted by Husyelt at Mount Eshki, he obeyed the god by bowing his face into his fire. His wife was Esmenet, with whom he had a son named Oresh.A half-Scylvendi, half-Norsirai woman of the Utemot and the favorite wife of Cnaiür urs Skiötha. Their children include a daughter named Sanathi. Cnaiür prizes Anissi above his other wives for enduring his harshness while continuing to love him.A Ciphrang—a demonic agency of the Outside—and one of the more manageable Potents controlled by the Scarlet Spires. In material form it is a writhing abomination with knife-like scales, limbs compared to iron pillars, an elephantine head, and a vast mouth encircled by eyes.A famed Norsirai commentator from Kûniüri and high priest of Gilgaöl.The Sapatishah-Governor of Gedea, whose totem is the Black Gazelle.The Nilnameshi king of Invishi during the fourteenth century of the Year-of-the-Tusk.Grandmaster of the Mandate during the Great Ordeal and an Exalt-Magus. Apart from Kellhus and Serwa, he is the only sorcerer rumored to have successfully recited a metagnostic cant.A Meöri High King who commissioned the Nausk Mausoleum to protect his soul from the Outside.A Nansur general who commands the Nasueret Column of the Imperial Army and follows Ikurei Conphas.One of Anasûrimbor Kellhus's bodyguards, mentioned by Nersei Proyas in a letter to his father, Nersei Eukernas II.The portly Nansur Prime Augur to Ikurei Xerius III and the emperor's favored augur and astrologer.A famed missionary priest of the Three Seas.The author of Six Ontonomies.A Tydonni Norsirai, client thane of Earl Rilding Werijen Greatheart, and one of the Nascenti.An Ainoni Ketyai, client of Sirpal Uranyanka, and member of the Holy War.A member of the Skin Eaters.A concubine of Anasûrimbor Nau-Cayûti, remembered in accounts surrounding the ancient struggle against Golgotterath.One of the leaders of the Cond tribesmen during the Second Age.An emperor of the Pseudo-Ûmeri Empire.An Inchoroi prince and twin brother of Aurax, remembered by different peoples under several names and titles.An Inchoroi prince and twin brother of Aurang, associated with the Tekne.One of the Cûnuroi remaining in Ishterebinth by 4132.A legendary Norsirai empress of the Ûmeri Empire in Far Antiquity and daughter of Wulta-Ongorean.A Nilnameshi lord of the Great Ordeal.A woman associated with House Gaunum, presumed to have served as a concubine in its household during the same period as Serwë.A Werigdan warrior, husband of Valrissa and father of Bengulla.A Scylvendi warrior of the Utemot tribe, son of Kututha and brother-in-law of Cnaiür urs Skiötha.A Scylvendi warrior of the Utemot tribes, son of Hannut, brother of Skiötha urs Hannut, and uncle of Cnaiür urs Skiötha.An Ordealman from Sepa-Gielgath.A member of the Company of Scions in the Great Ordeal.One of the Skin Eaters' mules, named by Mimara.A Nansur general who commands the Selial Column during the Holy War.A member of the Stone Hags.The Werigdan Norsirai son of Aëngelas and Valrissa.A Tydonni Norsirai soldier, member of the Holy War, and devout believer in the divinity of Anasûrimbor Kellhus.An Ordealman and New Imperial Consul of Ce Tydonn.Patridomos of House Biaxi during the events of The Prince of Nothing.Patridomos of House Biaxi during the Aspect-Emperor era and an important member of the New Congregate.A Nansur nobleman and the second Knight-Commander of the Shrial Knights during the Holy War.A Nansur general of the Kidruhil and eldest son of Biaxi Coronsas, Patridomos of House Biaxi.General of the Nansur contingent of the Great Ordeal.A Nilnameshi cook employed in the Andiamine Heights.A king of the Meöri Empire whose reign began in 1021.A king of the Meöri Empire and grandson of Borswelka I.A king of the Meöri Empire and father of Engûs.A Galeoth Norsirai nobleman and Earl of Agmundr during the Holy War.The god of famine and one of the Punitive Gods, who command sacrifice through threats and suffering. He has no formal cult or priesthood. Kiünnat tradition names him as Anagkë's elder brother, so Anagkean priests administer his rites of propitiation during times of hunger.A Kianene woman who serves as one of Esmenet's body-slaves.A Norsirai writer of the Ceneian Empire in Near Antiquity.A fanatical Ordealman known as the Candlemaker.An Ainoni sorcerer of rank in the Scarlet Spires.An elderly soldier and customer of Esmenet.The Nilnameshi Ketyai Grandmaster of the Vokalati, the feared sorcerous School known as the Sun-wailers of Nilnamesh.A Trysean God-King remembered for his jealousy toward Tynwur.The third Norsirai God-King of the Ûmeri Empire during the Nonman Tutelage and founder of the original Library of Sauglish.A famed philosopher and historian of Near Antiquity, best known for his authoritative work The Annals of Cenei.An Exalt-General stationed in Momemn during the Great Ordeal.A ruler of the Ûmeri Empire who faced Aulyanau the Conqueror at the Battle of River Axau.The Shiropti Grandmaster of the Imperial Saik during the Holy War.An Erratic Nonman Siqû and powerful Qûya, known in Kûniüric as Mekeritrig, the Traitor of Men.A Cûnuroi prince of Siöl, son of King Cu'huriol and father of Cû'jara-Cinmoi.A famed Shrial commentator, author of The Ten Holies, and tutor in exoterics to Nersei Proyas.A prince of Cingulat and member of the Company of Scions in the Great Ordeal.A Galeoth caste-noble who serves as a Judge in the Great Ordeal.The Ainoni King-Regent of High Ainon and nominal leader of the Ainoni during much of the First Holy War.An orphaned Ainoni Ketyai boy employed as a runner by Drusas Achamian in High Ainon. Outside that service, he survives through prostitution.An Injori Qûya called the Lord of Swans, renowned for confronting Murathaur the Silver.The first recorded child of mixed Man and Cûnuroi parentage, as preserved in the Isûphiryas. A daughter of the Emwama man Sirwitta, she was accepted and raised among the Cûnuroi.A famed Kianene Ketyai Sapatishah-Governor of Eumarna, known among his people as the Tiger of Eumarna, and father of Inrilil ab Cinganjehoi.A well-known Erratic Nonman and father of Immiriccas. The Four Revelations of Cinial’jin is told from his point of view.A legendary Siölan Ishroi and the strongest of the Nonmen, renowned for his struggles against great foes during the Cûno-Inchoroi Wars.Captain of the Inchausti during the Great Ordeal.A Scylvendi warrior and chieftain of the Utemot tribe.The unnamed first wife of Skiötha urs Hannut and mother of Cnaiür urs Skiötha.An Ordealman and the youngest son of Coithus Narnol.Daughter of Coithus Eryeat, sister of Coithus Narnol and Coithus Saubon, and mother of Coithus Athjeäri.The Galeoth Earl of Gaenri and nephew of Coithus Saubon. Regarded as the eyes of the Holy War, he scouts ahead with his men and reports on the Fanim.The Norsirai king of Galeoth during the Holy War and father of Coithus Narnol, Coithus Saubon, and Coithus Asilda.An Ordealman and Believer-King of Galeoth, eldest surviving son of Coithus Eryeat and brother of Coithus Saubon and Coithus Asilda.The seventh son of King Coithus Eryeat of Galeoth and titular leader of the Galeoth contingent in the First Holy War.The Kianene Grandee of Mizrai, famed for his enormous strength and size.A member of the Skin Eaters.The Earl of Pikka and general of the Cengemi in the Great Ordeal.The author of Nilnameshi Lore.A High King of Akksersia mentioned in The Sagas.The New Imperial Consul of Nansur and a political rival of Esmenet.A Nansur Ketyai Knight-Commander of the Shrial Knights during the Holy War.The Kianene Ketyai Sapatishah-Governor of Khemema.One of the Cûnuroi remaining in Ishterebinth by 4132.A Siölan Nonman Qûya and kinsman of Cû'jara-Cinmoi.The Cûnuroi king of Siöl before Arkfall, father of Cet'moyol and Linqirû, and grandfather of Cû'jara-Cinmoi.An Injori Ishroi known as Dragon-gored and the Lord Limper.A Tydonni Norsirai thane and one of the Nascenti.A Nonman remembered and called out for by Cleric in Cil-Aujas.The first God-King of Trysë, famed for conquering the cities of the River Aumris and forging the first treaty between Men and Nonmen.The greatest of the Nonman kings, High King of Siöl, and first great foe of the Inchoroi. He is the son of Cet'moyol and Linqirû and husband of Hanalinqû.The Tydonni Norsirai Earl of Cuärweth and a member of the Holy War.A Siölan Ishroi who, after observing an itinerant Sranc camp from concealment, famously argued that the Sranc possessed social customs and regimes nearly as complex as those of the Cûnuroi.A sorcerer of the Imperial Saik.A Mihtrûlic Grandmaster regarded as the most gifted sorcerous artificer among Men.Drusas Achamian's mule.A Sakarpi baron.Shriah of the Thousand Temples from 3371 to 3383, notorious for cruel excesses. His reign prompted the high clergy to issue the Writ of Psata-Antyu, limiting the authority of future Shriahs.A captain of Attrempus and lifelong comrade-in-arms to Krijates Xinemus.Two of Sanumnis's Chorae bowmen.The Tydonni Norsirai Earl of Sumagalt and a member of the Holy War.The author of Rudiments.A Sakarpi priest of Gilgaöl.A Nroni Ketyai former Mandate Schoolman and spy. During the Holy War he investigates the Scarlet Spires and the Thousand Temples. He bears the titles Holy Tutor, Vizier, and Wizard.A Galeoth Norsirai former thane and Shield-Captain of the Hundred Pillars.The Sapatishah-Governor of Holy Amoteu, regarded by the Inrithi as a tyrant.An Ordealman and sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires.The first institutional Shriah of the Thousand Temples and author of the widely admired 44 Epistles.A Shriah of the Thousand Temples, known as the Golden. His conversion of Triamis the Great helped establish Inrithism as the official religion of the Ceneian Empire.A Shriah of the Thousand Temples who prohibited art that, in his words, blasphemed the Simple, the Pure, and the True through foul Complication.A Shriah of the Thousand Temples and author of 111 Aphorisms.A Shriah of the Thousand Temples associated with the beginning of the Scholastic Wars.A High Priestess of the Cult of Yatwer during the early Great Ordeal.A legendary Siölan progenitor of the Qûya.The nurse of Anasûrimbor Kelmomas, replacing Porsi.An Ordealman and Angle-Thane of Scolow.An Ordealman famed for his monstrous stature.An Ishoriöl Nonman Siqû and founder of the Mihtrûl School of Contrivers. He is famed as the creator of powerful sorcerous artifacts, including several of the Sublime Contrivances.A Kûniüric Norsirai general in Anasûrimbor Celmomas II's Great Ordeal and husband of Ginsil. He is famed for victory at the Battle of Skothera.The fifth son of Borswelka IV, associated with the loss of Swur Fords and the Demua Mountains.A Siölan Cûnuroi, younger son of Cinial'jin and presumed son of Aisarinqu, and brother of Immiriccas and Aisralu.The Tydonni Norsirai Earl of Numaineiri during the Holy War.A Nroni judge in the Great Ordeal.A groom in the House Gaunum household.An Imperial cartographer during the reign of Ikurei Xerius III.A Galeoth Norsirai slave-girl belonging to Cutias Sarcellus.The author of The Ten Thousand Day Dynasty, a history of House Sorgis in Nansur.The Conriyan Ketyai Palatine of Annand.A member of the Stone Hags.A Ceneian historian and author of On the Arrangement of Souls in Battle and War.A Believer-King of Cironj and leader of the Cironji contingent in the Great Ordeal.A Ketyai woman from Sumna, friend and lover of Drusas Achamian, and wife of Anasûrimbor Kellhus.A historical figure in The Chronicle of the Tusk, wife of Angeshraël and mother of Oresh.A Lord of the Great Ordeal.A Kianene woman who serves as one of Esmenet's body-slaves.The first-born son of Kascamandri ab Tepherokar and leader of the Coyauri, Kian's famed elite heavy cavalry.A Nansur Ketyai prophet of the Solitary God, founder of Fanimry, and the first of the Cishaurim.An Indara-Kishauri Ketyai Cishaurim and one of the Nine Incandati, the most powerful Cishaurim.The eldest son of Fane and the first Padirajah of Kian.A Kianene Ketyai Padirajah who led the Dagger Jihad in 3933.A great Invitic Inrithi critic of Fanimry.Chieftain of one of the tribal companies of Scalpoi.Mimara's mule.An Orthodox agitator and proadjunct from the Selial Column.A Cepaloran Norsirai Exalt-Captain of the Palatial Eöthic Guard during the Holy War.An Ordealman, Lord of Agansanor, and cousin of King Hoga Hogrim.A Ceneian slave-scholar celebrated for commentaries on The Chronicle of the Tusk, collected as Contemplations on the Indentured Soul.A member of the Skin Eaters and former Nansur Columnary.A legendary Shiradi king featured in the Fable of Gam.An Imperial Scrollmaster of the Andiamine Heights.A person called out for by the unnamed Bloody Pick in Cil-Aujas.One of the Cûnuroi remaining in Ishterebinth by 4132.A man whose Third Revelation refers to the One Hundred and Forty-Four Thousand.One of the Lords of the Holy War.A member of House Gaunum during Serwë's time as a concubine.A son of House Gaunum's Patridomos and the father of Serwë's first child.A member of the Imperial Army at the Battle of Kiyuth.A Cepaloran Norsirai Exalt-Captain of the Eöthic Guard of the New Empire.A Consult skin-spy.One of the leaders of the Vulgar Holy War.An Ainoni Ketyai Shield-Captain of the Javreh.An ancient Wracu spawned during the Cûno-Inchoroi Wars.The goddess of carnal passion and one of the Compensatory Gods. Her cult is popular across the Three Seas, especially among aging men drawn to aphrodisica. In the Mar’eddat, she is the wife of Ajokli.The god of war and conflict, one of the Compensatory Gods, and the second most popular of the Hundred Gods after his sister Yatwer. His cult is harsh and demanding, with a substantial priesthood and many sacrificial offerings.A Kûniüric Norsirai woman and wife of General En-Kaujalau, remembered in The Sagas.A Nonman Ishroi and great hero of the ancient Mansion of Viri, remembered for opposing Nin’janjin and his Inchoroi allies at the Battle of Pir Pahal.A Nonman king of Cil-Aujas during the Apocalypse and teacher of Sos-Praniura.An ancient Kûniüric Norsirai poet famed for the Epic of Sauglish.An Ordealman and sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires.A Conriyan Ketyai baron from the Ainoni frontier during the Holy War.A Tydonni Norsirai thane of Hagmeir in Numaineiri.An Ordealman and Shield-Thane of King Hoga Hogrim, known as the Bald.A notorious Thunyeri Norsirai pirate and Earl of Cern Auglai.An Ordealman and Invitic knight.A great Ûmeri Norsirai sorcerer credited with separating philosophy from purely theological speculation.A great Kianene Fanim architect.A Shigeki slave of House Gaunum and friend of Serwë.An Ordealman and famed caste-menial champion of the Sranc Pits.An Ordealman and Ingraul swordsman from the High Wernma.A Swayali witch promoted to Grandmistress in Serwa's absence.High Cultist of Gilgaöl in the Holy War.The first organizer of the Coyauri, the Kianene Padirajah's elite heavy cavalry, formed in response to the Nansur Kidruhil.An Indara-Kishauri Ketyai Cishaurim and one of the Nine Incandati, the most powerful Cishaurim.A Ciphrang known as the Feathered Worm of the Pit.A slave famed among the Conriyan caste-nobility as a healer of troubled souls.An Ordealman and sorcerer of the Mysunsai.A Nansur Ketyai former blacksmith and one of the Nascenti.A famed Kianene Ketyai poet and successor to Tatokar I as Padirajah of Kian.A Prince of Erras and general of the Famiri in the Great Ordeal.A member of the Skin Eaters.A renowned Ainoni Ketyai dramatist remembered for Tempiras the King and his jnanic wit.A Kianene Fanim lord who fights in the battle for Shimeh.A high-ranking Imperial Apparati.Captain of Ikurei Conphas's bodyguard.A legendary Siölan Nonman and wife of Cû'jara-Cinmoi.The Ainoni Ketyai Grandmaster of the Scarlet Spires during the Holy War.The officially sanctioned Ketyai Matriarch of the Cult of Yatwer.A Galeoth Norsirai slave-girl belonging to Cutias Sarcellus.An Ordealman and Satrap of Tendant’heras.Lord Torturer of Ishterebinth under Nin'ciljiras.The Tydonni Norsirai Earl of Gaethuni during the Holy War.A Scylvendi warrior and eldest living son of Oknai One-Eye.Commander of Asgilioch during the Holy War.A Kianene warrior and eldest son of Skauras ab Nalajan.The infamous author of Exhortations, a work that rejects traditional Inrithi values in favor of unprincipled self-promotion.An Ordealman and cousin of Nemukus Mirshoa.One of three Tydonni brothers who owned the Cocked Leg inn in Marrow.A king who founded Ce Tydonn in 3741.A Scylvendi Utemot memorialist in Cnaiür urs Skiötha's childhood.A grizzled Kianene Fanim veteran who serves at Gerotha.A scholar known for opinions on the Holy War and the Unification Wars.A sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires during the Holy War.A historian noted for views on the Unification Wars, especially the Sack of Sarneveh.An Ordealman, Prince of Girgash, and eldest son of King Urmakthi.The ranking high priest of Akkeägni during the First Holy War.An Ainoni Ketyai Daimotic sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires and Master of Spies to Hanamanu Eleäzaras.The Breath-father of Thurror Eryelk.A witch of the Swayal Sisterhood in the Great Ordeal.A member of the Stone Hags.An orphaned Nansur boy living in Sumna, called Hertata-tata and Echo for repeating the final words of his sentences.One of the two named authors of The Sagas.The Galeoth Norsirai Earl of Nergaöta and one of the leaders of the Vulgar Holy War.An Ordealman and sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires.An Indara-Kishauri Ketyai Cishaurim sorcerer-priest and servant of Anasûrimbor Moënghus.The author of Five Apprehensions.A member of the Stone Hags.A former Mandate Court Advisor in the New Empire.The protagonist of The Book of Hintarates, one of the books of the Tusk.An Ordealman and Earl of Canute.The Ainoni Ketyai Palatine of Eshkalas during the Holy War.A Ciphrang known as the Great-Jawed Glutton.A member of the Skin Eaters.A Tydonni Norsirai and second-eldest son of Earl Hoga Gothyelk.A Tydonni Norsirai and eldest son of Earl Hoga Gothyelk.The Tydonni Norsirai Earl of Agansanor and leader of the Tydonni contingent in the Holy War.A Tydonni Norsirai and youngest son of Earl Hoga Gothyelk.An Ordealman, Believer-King of Ce Tydonn, and nephew of Hoga Gothyelk.A legendary Scylvendi Utemot King-of-Tribes and one of the greatest conquerors in Scylvendi history.A man mentioned in writing on a post at the outskirts of Marrow.A notorious Xerashi criminal mentioned in The Tractate.A king of High Ainon associated with the end of the Scholastic Wars and the rise of Scarlet Spires influence over High Ainon.One of the mannish translators and chroniclers of the Nonmen.The Priapic God.A caste-menial Zaudunyani agitator known as Rash.A Thunyeri Norsirai prince, second son of King Hringa Rauschang, called the Limper for his uneven gait.The first King of the Thunyeri, elected by the tribes in 3987.A Thunyeri Norsirai warrior and cousin of Prince Hringa Skaiyelt.A Thunyeri Norsirai prince and youngest son of King Hringa Rauschang.A Thunyeri Norsirai king and father of Princes Skaiyelt, Hulwarga, and Narradha.A Thunyeri Norsirai prince, eldest son of King Hringa Rauschang, and leader of the Thunyeri contingent in the Holy War.An Ordealman, Believer-King of Thunyerus, and son of Hringa Skaiyelt.An Ordealman and baron.The god of the hunt and one of the Compensatory Gods. His cult is especially popular in the Middle-North, and his high-ranking priests are rumored to wield significant wealth and political influence.The Kianene Ketyai Prince of Mongilea.A young sorcerer seen in Drusas Achamian's Dreams of the Apocalypse.An ancient Norsirai king of Sakarpus mentioned in The Sagas.A witch of the Swayal Sisterhood in the Great Ordeal.A Cûnuroi smith who forged the blade Holol during the Cûno-Inchoroi Wars.A Galeoth Norsirai slave of Drusas Achamian, an even-tempered man who makes regular visits to Marrow to trade pelts and secure provisions.A Holca Lord of the Great Ordeal.A Ketyai emperor of Nansur from 4066 to 4081 and grandfather of Ikurei Xerius III.A Ketyai nephew of Emperor Ikurei Xerius III and heir apparent to the Imperial Mantle.The unnamed younger son of Ikurei Istriya, brother of Ikurei Xerius III, and father of Ikurei Conphas.The unnamed half-sister of Ikurei Conphas and wife of Ikurei Xerius III.A Ketyai Empress of Nansur, mother of Ikurei Xerius III, once famed for legendary beauty.The first emperor of the Ikurei Dynasty in Nansur and a former Exalt-General.A Ketyai emperor of Nansur during the Holy War and uncle of Ikurei Conphas.The unnamed husband of Ikurei Istriya, father of Ikurei Xerius III, and predecessor to his son as emperor.The protagonist of a Zeümi folk tale.A presumed child of Aëngelas and Valrissa.A likely historian noted for opinions on the Unification Wars.A Kianene Sapatishah-Governor of Enathpaneah and son-in-law of Padirajah Kascamandri ab Tepherokar.The progenitor and father-creator of the Nonmen in Nonman tradition, from whom all Nonmen descend.A son of Cinial'jin.A Shigeki Lord of the Great Ordeal.A sorcerer of the Imperial Saik and author of The Psûkalogues.A Cepaloran Norsirai general of the Cepaloran Auxiliaries.A Siölan hero associated with Min-Uroikas.Grandmaster of the Shrial Knights and Maithanet's representative in the Holy War.A Cepaloran Norsirai and father of Serwë.A Nonman Ishroi hero of Siöl mentioned in the Isûphiryas.A far antique Kûniüric philosopher, famed for Dialogia and known in the Three Seas through Ajencis's critique of his Theosis.An Old Dynasty Shigeki Ketyai God-King who conquered the Kyranae Plains.An Indara-Ki