n Ordealman and Grandmaster of the Mysunsai.The founder of the Vokalati.One of the younger sons of Yursalka.A Nonman, son of the hero Oirûnas, and a Siqû.Father of Oirûnas and Oirinas.An Ishroi hero and twin brother of Oirûnas.A legendary Ishroi hero, dispossessed son of Siöl, twin brother of Oirinas, and Lord of the Second Watch.A Scylvendi Utemot warrior and cousin of Cnaiür urs Skiötha.The chieftain of the Munuäti, a powerful federation of Scylvendi tribes.A Scylvendi warrior and cousin of Cnaiür urs Skiötha.A Ceneian slave-scholar of Cironji descent, famed for Avowals.A legendary daughter of Imimorûl and sister of Tsonos.The lame daughter of Xunnurit and wife of Yursalka.A Kianene Grandee and follower of Fanayal ab Kascamandri.The first woman according to The Chronicle of the Tusk.The goddess of hope and aspiration.A near antique Ceneian satirist best known for On the Folly of Men.A near antique Cengemian moralist best known for On the Carnal.A Kianene slave who served as the infant Anasûrimbor Moënghus II's wet nurse.A historical figure in The Chronicle of the Tusk and youngest son of Angeshraël and Esmenet.Possibly the god of sleep.A plump scullery slave of the House Gaunum household.A Sakarpi hero famed for racing on foot from the Pale to the Lonely City to give warning of a vast mobbing.An Ordealman and Baron of Low Kalt.A member of the Stone Hags.A Far Antique king of Trysë associated with overthrowing the Cond Yoke.The son of Lord Ostaroot.A Scylvendi warrior who fought in the Battle of Kiyuth.A sorcerer of the Imperial Saik during the Holy War.A famed Sohonc metaphysician and central figure of the Gnostic Renaissance.A member of the Skin Eaters and renegade son of Yalgrota Sranchammer.Captain of the Stone Hags and a Mysunsai Schoolman.An Old Dynasty God-King of Shigek who raised a Ziggurat of Shigek bearing his name.A sorcerer notably aligned with Orthodox movements.A Scylvendi of the Munuäti tribe.A philosopher, likely a student of Ajencis, and author of