atinate of Aderot during the Holy War.One of the Nine Incandati, the most powerful Cishaurim.A Believer-Prince of Nilnamesh, general of the Nilnameshi contingent in the Great Ordeal, and son of Sasal Umrapathur III.A Believer-King of Nilnamesh and Marshal of the Ketyai-of-the-South in the Great Ordeal.A Grandmaster of the Scarlet Spires.A former Ainoni baron and one of the Nascenti.A sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires during the Holy War.The Thunyeri Earl of Skagwa during the Holy War.A member of the Stone Hags.A senior member of the Mandate Quorum.Count-Palatine of the Ainoni palatinate of Hinnant during the Holy War.The author of Sumni Meditations.A Nymbricani concubine of House Gaunum.A figure appearing as Serwë.Founder of the Mandate School and enemy of the Consult during the Apocalypse.A Ciphrang controlled by the Scarlet Spires at the battle for Shimeh.General commanding the Ainoni contingent of the First Holy War.Heresiarch of the Cishaurim.Grandvizier of the Mangaecca.A Javreh Shield-Captain serving Hanamanu Eleäzaras.A historical figure in The Chronicle of the Tusk and mother of Esmenet (Tusk).A High-Priestess of the Cult of Yatwer.A former Tydonni thane and one of the Nascenti.One of the Chieftain-Kings named in the Tusk.The Tydonni Earl of Warnute during the Holy War.The son of Earl Sheorog Cerjulla and a member of the Holy War.King of ancient Xerash, remembered in The Tractate.An Ordealman and Tydonni Earl of Cuärweth.One of the mannish translators and chroniclers of the Nonmen.The eldest son of Shoddû Rapita III and a notable Orthodox general in the Unification Wars.A king of Nilnamesh during the Unification Wars and father of Shoddû Akirapita.An Ordealman and Exalt-Captain of the Pillarians.A Galeoth Ordealman from Agmundr.Count-Palatine of the Conriyan palatinate of Anplei during the Holy War.An Orthodox Palatine of Etara-Anplei.An emperor of Cenei associated with the suppression of a rebellion in Kyudea.A Believer-Prince of Nymbrica and leader of the Cepaloran contingent in the Great Ordeal.An Inchoroi king and the original bearer of the Heron Spear.Daughter of Idrusus Geraus and Tisthanna, Drusas Achamian's Galeoth slaves.A Javreh Shield-Captain and favorite of Hanamanu Eleäzaras.A Nonman king of Nihrimsûl and Ishoriöl, and father of Nil'giccas.A supporter of House Ikurei and Exalt-General of the Nansurium before Ikurei Conphas.The youngest daughter of Kascamandri ab Tepherokar.An Ordealman and Lord Palatine of Moserothu.Palatine-Governor of the Ainoni city of Moserothu during the Holy War.A Seleukaran poet, naturalist, philosopher, and author of The Holy Crone.An Emwama criminal mentioned in the Isûphiryas.One of the principal Wracu of the Apocalypse.A Thunyeri chieftain who fought alongside Cnaiür urs Skiötha at Joktha.Gaenkelti's successor as Exalt-Captain of the Palatial Eöthic Guard.A Mysunsai Schoolman during the Holy War.Sapatishah-Governor of Shigek and an early principal antagonist of the First Holy War.Prime Counsel to Ikurei Xerius III.A Tydonni thane and member of the Holy War.Father of Cnaiür urs Skiötha and former chieftain of the Utemot.An ancient Wracu associated with the Cûno-Inchoroi Wars.An Ordealman, Scylvendi scout, and Knight of the Desert Lion.An ancient Wracu called the Black.A Girgallic priest from Varalt Sorweel's childhood.A Ciphrang controlled by the Scarlet Spires during the battle for Shimeh.The author of Ten Seasons in Zeüm.An orphan living in Sumna during the Holy War.A former Tydonni thane and one of the Nascenti.A Nilnameshi caste-noble adventurer and member of the Skin Eaters.A Galeoth knight and client of Coithus Saubon.A celebrated Nansur scriptural commentator and author of The Book of Circles and Spirals.The greatest student of Gin'yursis and founder of the Mangaecca.An Ordealman and High-Thane of the Holca.An Ordealman and Lord Palatine of Kethantei, the second son of Sristai Ingiaban.Palatine of the Conriyan palatinate of Kethantei during the Holy War.A Ceneian Philosopher-Emperor and author of Ruminations.A pony owned by Varalt Sorweel after he joined the Great Ordeal.A Nonman Qûya rumored to have performed Meta-Gnostic Cants.A legendary king of Sakarpus.Earl of Gaenri and commander of the Gaenrish contingent in the Great Ordeal.An Ordealman and Kianene Grandee of Mitirabis.A queen of High Ainon during the Scholastic Wars and wife of Sarothesser IX.Wife of Anasûrimbor Celmomas II and mother of Anasûrimbor Nau-Cayûti.A Nansur Surmante emperor noted for diplomacy and reforms to the Nansur legal code.A Surmante emperor of Nansur associated with the Granary Revolts.A warlike Surmante emperor of Nansur who expanded the empire.The youngest son of Pilaskanda and leader of Fanayal ab Kascamandri's embassy to Momemn.An Imperial Exalt-Counter.A member of the Skin Eaters and rumored Fanim heretic.The author of Epimeditations.The Galeoth Earl of Kurigald during the Holy War.According to legend, the son of Nostol and Weyukat.Sapatishah-Governor of Jurisada.A legendary maiden associated with the origin of the Swayal Sisterhood.A Skettic chieftain associated with Avalunsil.An Injori Ishroi, dispossessed son of Siöl, known in the Three Seas as the Red Ghoul.An ancient Wracu called the Red.Admiral of the Nansur Fleet during the Holy War.A High Heresiarch of the Cishaurim.Grandmaster of the Imperial Saik in the Great Ordeal.A renowned theologian of the early Thousand Temples.The Galeoth Earl of Gesindal during the Holy War.Patridomos of House Thallei and general of the Kidruhil during the Holy War.An Ordealman, Mandate Schoolman, and tutor to Varalt Sorweel.A ranking member of the Imperial Saik.An unnamed Norsirai initiate of the Dûnyain, son of Anasûrimbor Koringhus and grandson of Anasûrimbor Kellhus.A group of five Dûnyain associated with Ishuäl.An Amoti Ordealman, Knight of the Desert Lion, and swordbearer to Coithus Saubon.An Ordealman and sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires.Eunuch Master of Imperial Protocol for the New Empire.A late Ceneian dramatist famed for Triamis Imperator.A Holca Ordealman, Knight of the Desert Lion, and spearbearer to Coithus Saubon.A Holca freebooter famed as both a hero and criminal during the Scholastic Wars.A sorcerer of the Scarlet Spires during the Holy War.An Ordealman and Grandee of Makreb'at-Akii.A Nonman who fought beside Cinial'jin during the Cûno-Inchoroi Wars.A Scylvendi of the Akkunihor tribe and member of the Company of Scions in the Great Ordeal.A former Nansur slave of the Kianene.A baron and member of the Holy War.Drusas Achamian's slave and wife of Idrusus Geraus.The second Grandmaster of the Sohonc, pupil of Noshainrau the White, and famed Hero-Mage of Ûmerau.Master of Spies to Ikurei Xerius III.The first Aspect-Emperor of Cenei, known for his conquests and declaration of Inrithism as the state religion.Patridomos of House Trimus during the Holy War.A Trimus emperor of Nansur.Captain of the Hemscilvara.A former Kutnarmu mercenary and one of the Nascenti.The author of The Sumptitudes.A Qûya queen of Ishoriöl, wife of Sin'niroiha, and mother of Nil'giccas.Son of Imimorûl and legendary Ur-King of Siöl.A Grandmaster of the Scarlet Spires, then known as the Surartu, in ancient times.A Consult skin-spy.An Ordealman and senior Imperial mathematician.Known as the Bull of Sauglish.A Jekki member of the Company of Scions in the Great Ordeal.A member of the Stone Hags.An ancient Shiradic philosopher.An Ordealman and younger brother of Urbommû Hamazrel.An Ordealman and one of Nurbanu Soter's martial advisors.An Ordealman and Palatine of Kûtapileth.A Believer-King of Girgash and leader of the Girgashi contingent in the Great Ordeal.A Ciphrang known as Father-of-Carrion.A so-called Sranc King of Suskara.One of the Chieftain-Kings named in the Tusk.Sapatishah-Governor of Xerash during the Holy War.A Scylvendi King-of-Tribes.A daughter of the Werigda and wife of Aëngelas.A witch of the Swayal Sisterhood in the Great Ordeal.A former king of Sakarpus and father of Varalt Sorweel III.A king of Sakarpus and only son of Varalt Harweel II.The unnamed wife of Varalt Harweel II and mother of Varalt Sorweel III.Grandmaster of the Imperial Saik and Vizier-in-Proxy.A Chalfantic Oracle of the Cult of Yatwer.A dispossessed son of Siöl and a Qûya.An arcane Siölan smith who forged Imirsiöl, the legendary blade of Oirûnas.A mighty Inchoroi associated with the Cûno-Inchoroi Wars.An Ordealman and Ingraulish knight.A client thane of Hoga Gothyelk during the First Holy War and later an Ordealman.A Kûniüric prince who took part in the Second Ordeal at the Battle of Eleneöt Fields.Earl of the Tydonni fiefdom of Canute during the Holy War.The favored Emwama concubine of Gin'yursis according to legend.A Yatwerian Narindar whose Unerring Grace is absolute.The legendary founder of the Holca.A senior member of the Mbimayu.A member of the Skin Eaters.An Ordealman and Earl of Nangaelsa.A King-Temple Historian known for theories about Sranc populations.A caste-menial Zaudunyani agitator.A member of the Stone Hags.A Far Antique Ûmeri emperor and father of Avalunsil.An Ordealman from Nangaelsa.The legendary Father of Dragons and an Unholy Archetype.A famed and maligned Satta Warlock, and master of Iswa.An Ordealman and Kidruhil captain of the Company of Scions.A Ceneian leader who secured the remnants of Kyraneas after Cenei's conquest of Gielgath.An Old Dynasty God-King of Shigek known for the Ziggurat bearing his name.A Ceneian poet and playwright famed for The Trucian Dramas.A member of the Skin Eaters and former Imperial Tracker.A Scylvendi chieftain of the Akkunihor tribe and King-of-Tribes at the Battle of Kiyuth.A Thunyeri Momian Patriarch.A Thunyeri groom to Prince Hringa Skaiyelt during the Holy War.The master of the Carythusal brothel where Mimara was found.A prostitute acquainted with Esmenet.A Mandate Schoolman and Quorum member during the Holy War.The goddess of earth and fertility.One of Esmenet's Kianene body-slaves.Mimara's Nilnameshi tutor during her time in the Andiamine Heights.A venerated Qûya sage.Son of Idrusus Geraus and Tisthanna, Drusas Achamian's Galeoth slaves.A slave belonging to the Gaunum family.The wife of Sag-Marmau in The Sagas, whose name is used as an euphemism for “adulteress” in the Three Seas.A Scylvendi warrior of the Utemot tribe.A Scylvendi King-of-Tribes at the Battle of Zirkirta.A sorcerer of rank in the Scarlet Spires during the Holy War.A longtime Grandmaster of the Mbimayu, scholar of Memgowa, and early master of Malowebi.The author of A Defence of the Arcane Arts.Captain of Attrempus during the Holy War and a former Nilnameshi slave of Krijates Xinemus's household.The first Zerxei emperor of Nansur.A Zerxei emperor of Nansur who had the High Round raised in Shimeh.A Zerxei emperor of Nansur.The women taken as concubines by Anasûrimbor Kellhus.A Ciphrang controlled by the Scarlet Spires during the battle for Shimeh.Successor-Prince of Zeüm and a member of the Company of Scions in the Great Ordeal.Wife of Oirûnas and mother of Oinaral Lastborn.The legendary founder of Ishoriöl and Incissal.A Consult skin-spy.A Kurigalder Ordealman, Knight of the Desert Lion, and shieldbearer to Coithus Saubon.